{"title":"Superagh's Olympiad Notes","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Introduction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introduction</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Algebra\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Algebra</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Inequalities\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inequalities</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Power_mean_(special_case)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Power mean (special case)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Power_mean_(weighted)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Power mean (weighted)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Bernoulli&#39;s_Inequality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Bernoulli's Inequality</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Rearrangement_Inequality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rearrangement Inequality</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Holder&#39;s_Inequality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Holder's Inequality</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Combinatorics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Combinatorics</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Number_Theory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Number Theory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Geometry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geometry</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introduction\">Introduction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Introduction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>SINCE MY COMPUTER WON'T LOAD THIS FOR SOME REASON, I'LL BE UPDATING THIS AS I GO THOUGH&#160;:)\n</p><p>Ok, so inspired by master math solver Lcz, I have decided to take Oly notes (for me) online! I'll probably be yelled at even more for staring at the computer, but I know that this is for my good. (Also this thing is almost the exact same format as Lcz's :P ). (Ok, actually, a LOT of credits to Lcz)\n</p><p>NEVERYMIND I\"M DOING THIS ON MY BLOG SINCE IT\"LL LOAD\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Algebra\">Algebra</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Algebra\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Problems worth noting/reviewing\nI'll leave this empty for now, I want to start on HARD stuff yeah!\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inequalities\">Inequalities</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Inequalities\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We shall begin with INEQUALITIES! They should be fun enough. I should probably begin with some theorems.\n</p>\n<h4><span id=\"Power_mean_.28special_case.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Power_mean_(special_case)\">Power mean (special case)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Power mean (special case)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Statement: Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/861678758a5b44b76c992ebcbd65294d56a46fce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, ... a_n &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a6c417c270cab2e9b2827c1c40f88163d171bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i} \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd77e67d5e894bf1026f4cffd551f2856f52af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. Define the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223922cea67011996a3b00a2033eeebc5055f847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pm_x(a_1, a_2, \\cdots , a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> as:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc47ff3b8f1015a599578cca800e555507e382c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{a_1^x+a_2^x+\\cdots+a_n^x}{n})^{\\frac{1}{x}},\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"36\" />where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef232f1c3f50a3c3557f43153502b25dec8d3bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, and:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dd19fdaf0686ffca569aceaf5f1ec2f02916f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[n]{a_{1}a_{2}a_{3} \\cdots a_{n}}.\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43a968ffad6077425cb637a389b5879fa52e872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, then<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a51f71d68c4e95c1e85575a6681d32c8ad46da0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[pm_x(a_1, a_2, \\cdots , a_n) \\ge pm_y(a_1, a_2, \\cdots , a_n).\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h4><span id=\"Power_mean_.28weighted.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Power_mean_(weighted)\">Power mean (weighted)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Power mean (weighted)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Statement: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edadafd4d8e9b69d90e12feabadfc254c40db9ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, . . . a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"11\" /> be positive real numbers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5511a15f02dafab26a431a4fc9c86d6a2f9b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_1, w_2, w_3, . . . w_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" /> be positive real numbers (\"weights\") such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e523b17be9e10fd8a72cf58d83aa34142a649c12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_1+w_2+w_3+ . . . w_n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"14\" />. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a98609f367cbfaa54a71d68ec7d635ed366d77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p><p>if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400365c088499af977542271fc6363b086a63499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=0$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/a/3fa5df45a1c9d7fef72606902a8ecdf595724e16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(r)=a_1^{w_1} a_2^{w_2} a_3^{w_3} . . . a_n^{w_n}\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddde7dd752b934381ecdc777b24c5156bdfd3a8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7877cd24ec9e5b0c3ddf4e3e2e4a7682b45611.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(r)=(w_1a_1^r+w_2a_2^r+w_3a_3^r . . . +w_na_n^r)^{\\frac{1}{r}}\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f33b4fadb0d70e770c03c0d0926c2418487928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&gt;s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec01a554e509e97cd657f71b189b729dc49b218e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(r) \\geq P(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />. Equality occurs if and only if all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> are equal.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Let there be two sets of integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded92281b06aca3ae95cd10e6d59bff7fa9a3c0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/287f19d7b2d8d97427d7047b5242c3886d29082e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\cdots b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, where all members of the sequences are real, then we have:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fcfff75bc84b8d68d0765ea27c3db91bc14ddf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1^2+a_2^2+\\cdots +a_n^2)(b_1^2+b_2^2+ \\cdots +b_n^2)\\ge (a_1b_1 + a_2b_2 + \\cdots +a_nb_n)^2.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"19\" />Equality holds if for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02ee80beb6889c1454155c58c394e6e2f2dbcbd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e21bbcc8b1a1db90a76c7cda79b37d049509a5a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, or for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02ee80beb6889c1454155c58c394e6e2f2dbcbd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c0448f25be090bdec5d33c581232934667a43e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />., or we have some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69d76c74df8f0bf4cff77857b0b389af012914e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=ka_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h4><span id=\"Bernoulli.27s_Inequality\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bernoulli's_Inequality\">Bernoulli's Inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Bernoulli&#39;s Inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/9238d82d59d5dfe79e96d916bfdf2f4acc4ed3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598558af63f732a4ed32e72489da46be4829226b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, we have:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f402ea827326e5e1dbf3be355d9532b80417e037.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+x)^n \\ge 1+nx.\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rearrangement_Inequality\">Rearrangement Inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Rearrangement Inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Given that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121fdf5fe52d51ad9c9f5948223d516d776370d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 \\ge x_2 \\ge x_3 \\cdots x_n\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />and<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f9221e038149a2f0c7f07d2dd1c84c9b1cbe3efe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_1 \\ge y_2 \\ge y_3 \\cdots y_n.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />We have:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c3be9ce07ae768291267d3bb74920d816de682.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1y_1+x_2y_2 + \\cdots + x_ny_n\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />is greater than any other pairings' sum.\n</p>\n<h4><span id=\"Holder.27s_Inequality\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Holder's_Inequality\">Holder's Inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Holder&#39;s Inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e047bc14560bc613b17fb1ba735bba221764510a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a258926ff9daba3d399f1be87dd4742595ceb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\cdots, b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087594ea26fa196b8e61bc20a36228270dc695f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128ff39fb4345802b64d71cf0a9fd687e8ed033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1, z_2, \\cdots, z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> are nonnegative real numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be7c6c5b96a9b8e810416aeeee5d86592772c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda_a, \\lambda_b, \\cdots, \\lambda_z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" /> are nonnegative reals with sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59ea837c546f57b45aa402158a2de87394950c36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1^{\\lambda_a}b_1^{\\lambda_b} \\cdots z_1^{\\lambda_z} + \\cdots + a_n^{\\lambda_a} b_n^{\\lambda_b} \\cdots z_n^{\\lambda_z} \\le (a_1 + \\cdots + a_n)^{\\lambda_a} (b_1 + \\cdots + b_n)^{\\lambda_b} \\cdots (z_1 + \\cdots + z_n)^{\\lambda_z} .\\]\" width=\"643\" height=\"20\" />This is a generalization of the Cauchy Swartz Inequality.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Combinatorics\">Combinatorics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Combinatorics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>ok look bro\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d86ee296c142d4b84c4e91927de035290e72c326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>lol\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f9d16285f8e9cbf693f053fd372b2d433a5adc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi{n} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{asdf}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Number_Theory\">Number Theory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Number Theory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geometry\">Geometry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Superagh%27s_Olympiad_Notes&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Geometry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>hahaha\n</p><p>geometry sucks\n</p><p>~Lcz 5:02 PM CST, 6/25/2020\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018111422\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 290/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9596/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18989:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018111422 and revision id 267508. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}